From c1791e8740dffeff556d2d6c7134c14e31401d5d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: energie-teilen <noreply@energie-teilen.de>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 20:49:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(engine): annual statement engine with exact cent
 reconciliation
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

shared/billing.ts turns measured quantities into per-participant
statements. It closes the chain the previous two engines started: the
metering concept says how it is measured, the allocation says who took
which kilowatt-hour, this says what each of them pays.

Money is integer cents end to end, and every total is the sum of the
amounts above it rather than an independent recomputation — a statement
whose line items do not add up to its total is worthless however good
the physics behind it was. reconcile() re-checks those identities from
the produced result alone, so a caller can assert the statement adds up
without trusting the code that made it; the API returns it in the
response.

Also computed: the standing charge prorated by day (with the convention
stated rather than applied silently), instalments netted off into a
balance that goes negative for a credit, each participant's shared
share, and the difference against full basic supply. Without the local
basic-supply price both that difference and the working-price
comparison are reported as undecidable rather than filled in with a
plausible number. The VAT rate carries its own unverified provenance.

- POST /api/v1/billing, listed in /api/v1/meta.
- BillingPreview inside the allocation panel: one household's year,
  where entering the single number only the visitor has — the local
  basic-supply price — turns the comparison from undecidable into a
  figure, and shows the cap comparison alongside it.

38 new tests; 348 total. Typecheck, tests and build clean.
